<InfoLayout title="Privacy and Analytics" description="Understand the current preview’s data practices: static educational pages, no enabled GA4 tracking, no account forms, and the scope of future local tools." eyebrow="Clear about what happens here" lead="This page describes the current preview. We will update it before enabling new data collection or production analytics.">
  <p class="small-label">Current implementation · 3 November 2026</p>
  <h2>The current preview</h2><p>The application serves static learning pages and fixed illustrations. It does not offer accounts, payment processing, an active contact form, or external game connections. The simulator and calculator are static previews and do not currently generate or store user outcome histories.</p>
  <h2>Analytics is not enabled</h2><p>No Google Analytics 4 script or analytics event collection has been enabled in this application. The current application does not set analytics cookies or use local storage for analytics preferences.</p><p>A future analytics integration will require explicit configuration, an appropriate consent experience, and updated disclosures before it is enabled. The planned events concern page and educational-tool engagement. We do not plan to send outcome histories, free-text questions, account details, or sensitive inputs as event data.</p>
  <h2>Website delivery still involves requests</h2><p>Opening a page sends a request to the server or hosting provider delivering it. Those systems can receive technical request information, such as an IP address, requested URL, and browser information. This is different from an application analytics event.</p><p>The production hosting configuration and any hosting-provider telemetry will be reviewed before launch. This preview is not a claim that all data remains on your device, or that a future host has no logs.</p>
  <h2>Local experiments, when available</h2><p>The planned tools will generate educational outcomes in the browser and keep the active run in memory. Replaying a recorded run will not create a new random sample. Export, if offered, will be a user-initiated local download. The actual behavior will be documented here when implemented.</p>
  <h2>Links to other websites</h2><p>Guides link to mathematical references and the versioned source of the selected example ruleset. Visiting an external website is a separate request governed by that site’s practices. External references are not endorsements of a gambling operator or prediction service.</p>
  <h2>Questions about privacy</h2><p>A public contact destination is pending. See the <a href="/contact/">contact information page</a> for its current status. Before the production launch, this notice will be reviewed against the actual hosting, contact, analytics, and consent configuration.</p>
</InfoLayout>
